[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000]   Good morning, ladies and gentlemen, and welcome to the Monroe, Inc.'s Earnings Conference Call for the third quarter of fiscal 2020.
[00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:17.000]   At this time, all participants are in a listen-only mode. Later, we will conduct a question-and-answer session, and instructions will follow at that time.
[00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.000]   If anyone should require assistance during the call, please press *0 on your touchtone phone.
[00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:29.000]   As a reminder, ladies and gentlemen, this conference is being recorded and may not be reproduced in whole or in part without permission from the company.
[00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:38.000]   I would now like to introduce Ms. Maureen Mulholland, Senior Vice President, General Counsel, and Secretary of Monroe. Thank you. Please go ahead.
[00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.000]   Thank you. Hello, everyone, and thank you for joining us on this morning's call.
[00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:58.000]   Before we get started, please note that as part of the call this morning, we will be referencing a presentation that is available on the Investors section of our website at corporate.monroe.com/investors/investors.
[00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:15.000]   If I could draw your attention to the Safe Harbor Statement on slide 2 of the presentation, I'd like to remind participants on this morning's call that our presentation includes some forward-looking statements about Monroe's future performance.
[00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:27.000]   Actual results may differ materially from those suggested by our comments today. The most significant factors that could affect future results are outlined in Monroe's filings with the SEC and in our earlier statements.
[00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:43.000]   The company disclaims any intention or obligation to update or revise any forward-looking statements, whether as a result of new information, future events, or otherwise, except as required by law.
[00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:56.000]   Additionally, on today's call, management statements include a discussion of certain non-GAAP financial measures, which are intended to supplement and not be substitutes for comparable GAAP measures.
[00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:06.000]   Reconciliations of such supplemental information to the comparable GAAP measures will be included as part of today's presentation and in our earnings release.
[00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:13.000]   With that, I'd like to turn the call over to our President and Chief Executive Officer, Brett Ponton. Brett?
[00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:25.000]   Thank you, Maureen, and good morning, everyone. Thanks for joining us. I'll get started today with a brief overview of our third quarter results, followed by an update on the progress we've made on our Monroe Forward strategy.
[00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:38.000]   As illustrated on slide 3, we reported comps down 0.9% in the third quarter as higher year-over-year ticket was offset by negative traffic.
[00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:44.000]   In October and the beginning of November, we performed well against difficult comparisons in the prior year.
[00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:51.000]   Mild weather conditions towards the end of November and end of December caused a slowdown across our core northern markets.
[00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.000]   These conditions have continued into January.
[00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.000]   With our comparable store sales down 4% during the month.
[00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.000]   We do not like talking about the weather.
[00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:06.000]   However, it is impossible to ignore the impact it has on our business.
[00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:13.000]   While we are not satisfied with our financial results this quarter, we are executing well against the areas within our control.
[00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:21.000]   In particular, we continue to move deeper into our company transformation and are confident we are on the right path.
[00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.000]   We are committed to making the necessary changes.
[00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:32.000]   Across our organization to position us to deliver strong results no matter the external circumstances.
[00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.000]   Moving on to our performance by category in the third quarter.
[00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.000]   We were down 1% year-over-year in tire comparable store sales.
[00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:45.000]   As higher ticket year-over-year was offset by a decline in tire volume.
[00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:52.000]   We experienced more normalized retail pricing this quarter and are focused on further refining our tire strategy.
[00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:56.000]   To drive strength in our largest category.
[00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:04.000]   Importantly, we are on track to roll out our tire category management and pricing system beginning in the first quarter of fiscal 2021.
[00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:09.000]   Which will enable a more dynamic and sophisticated approach to real-time pricing.
