[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.580]   Good morning, and welcome to the first quarter 2020 General Electric Company Earnings Conference
[00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:07.900]   Call.
[00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.580]   My name is Brandon, and I'll be your operator for today.
[00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:13.680]   At this time, all participants are in a listen-only mode.
[00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.060]   Later, we will conduct a question-and-answer session, during which you can dial star 1
[00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:18.900]   if you have a question.
[00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:24.140]   Please note this conference is being recorded, and I will now turn it over to Steve Winokur,
[00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.040]   Vice President of Investor Communications.
[00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.200]   You may begin, sir.
[00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.180]   Thanks, Brandon.
[00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:35.240]   Good morning, and welcome to GE's first quarter 2020 Earnings Call.
[00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:40.640]   I'm joined by our Chairman and CEO, Larry Culp, and CFO, Carolina Didekapa.
[00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:45.800]   Before we start, I'd like to remind you that the press release and presentation are available
[00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:46.560]   on our website.
[00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:51.100]   Note that some of the statements we're making are forward-looking and are based on our best
[00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.780]   view of the world and our businesses as we see them today.
[00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:58.920]   As described in our SEC filings and on our website, those elements can change as the
[00:00:58.920 --> 00:00:59.680]   world changes.
[00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.820]   With that, I'll hand the call over to Larry.
[00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:05.860]   Steve, thanks.
[00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:06.960]   Good morning, everyone.
[00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.980]   We hope you and your families are healthy and safe.
[00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:13.900]   Our thoughts are with all of those affected by this global pandemic.
[00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:19.000]   We recognize this is a very difficult and challenging time for everyone.
[00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:24.980]   On behalf of GE, I want to express our gratitude to those on the front lines in the medical
[00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:28.900]   community, many of whom we're privileged to call our customers.
[00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:32.180]   Working tirelessly to protect all of us.
[00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:33.620]   Thank you.
[00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:38.960]   When we last spoke during our Outlook call in March, we were encouraged by the continued
[00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:43.880]   strength in aviation and healthcare and the progress made in power and renewables.
[00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:47.860]   In the eight weeks since, the world has fundamentally changed.
[00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:55.160]   As we all know, the COVID-19 pandemic evolved rapidly, hitting hard and hitting fast.
[00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:59.560]   While this is an earnings call, our goal today is to provide you with the information you need to
[00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:04.680]   get the most current and relevant information we have, and as always, to be as open and
[00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.240]   transparent as we possibly can.
[00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:09.560]   So forgive us if we run a little long today.
[00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:16.840]   The COVID-19 dynamics at GE, like the economy at large, are fluid and still evolving, but
[00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.800]   clearly challenging in the near term.
[00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:22.900]   With that, I'll start with our response to COVID-19.
[00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:26.560]   Carolina, who is joining our earnings call for the first time, will cover the financials.
[00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:29.520]   Then I'll wrap with a more in-depth view.
[00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:59.540]   Thank you very much for your time, and I look forward to working with you in the future.
[00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:29.520]   Thank you.
[00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:34.060]   This includes temperature screenings, face coverings and gloves as necessary, and physical
[00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:38.380]   distancing, all keeping with national, state, and local guidelines.
[00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:43.880]   I'm also inspired by the support that our employees have shown each other.
[00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:49.720]   We recently established an employee relief fund, and more than 75 senior leaders across
[00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:54.840]   GE have contributed portions of their salary to support those affected by this crisis.
[00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:59.300]   Our second priority is continuing to serve our customers.
[00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:04.080]   In health care, we're ramping production of critical medical equipment used to diagnose
