[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.280]   Ladies and gentlemen, thank you for standing by and welcome to the SAG Third Quarter 2020 Earnings Conference Call.
[00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:11.440]   At this time, all participants are in a listen-only mode.
[00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.860]   Later, we will conduct a question-and-answer session and instructions will follow at that time.
[00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:21.020]   If anyone should require assistance during the conference, please press star zero on your touch-tone telephone.
[00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:24.000]   As a reminder, this conference call is being recorded.
[00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.120]   Thank you. I would like to turn the conference over to your host, Mr. Brendan Frey. Please go ahead.
[00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.040]   Thank you, Grace.
[00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:37.460]   Good afternoon and thank you for joining us today to review SAG's Third Quarter 2020 financial results.
[00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:43.440]   On the call today, we have Chris Ahern, Chief Executive Officer, and Taylor Smith, Chief Financial Officer.
[00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:49.380]   Following Chris and Taylor's prepared comments, we will open the call for a question-and-answer session.
[00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:56.400]   Our third quarter earnings press release was issued today after the market closed at approximately 4.05 p.m. Eastern Time.
[00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.540]   As a follow-on to the earnings release,
[00:00:58.540 --> 00:00:59.980]   we published a supplemental financial statement.
[00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.260]   We also furnished this document to the SEC on Form 8.
[00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:13.560]   You can find all our earnings documents on our Investor Relations website at zag.com in the Quarterly Results section under the Financials tab.
[00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:21.480]   We are recording this call and a podcast of the conference call will be archived at the SAG Investor Relations webpage under the Events tab for one year.
[00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:27.740]   Before we begin, we would like to remind everyone that the prepared remarks contain forward-looking statements
[00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.980]   and management may make additional comments.
[00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.460]   We will also like to remind everyone that the prepared remarks contain general forward-looking statements in response to your questions.
[00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:40.940]   These statements include, but are not limited to, our outlook for the company and statements that estimate or project future results of operations for the performance of the company.
[00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:45.620]   These statements do not guarantee future performance and speak as of the date hereof.
[00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:53.600]   For more detailed discussion on the factors that can cause actual results to differ materially from those projected in the forward-looking statements,
[00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:59.980]   we refer all of you to the risk factors contained in SAG's annual report on Form 10-K and quarterly results.
[00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.080]   For more detailed information on the factors contained in SAG's annual report on Form 10-Q, follow the Securities and Exchange Commission.
[00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:11.040]   SAG assumes no obligation to revise any forward-looking statements that may be made in today's release or call.
[00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:18.700]   Please note that on today's call, in addition to discussing the GAAP financial results, we will discuss adjusted EBITDA, a non-GAAP financial measure.
[00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:27.380]   Explanation of SAG's use of this non-GAAP financial measure in this call and reconciliation between GAAP and non-GAAP measures required by SEC Regulation G
[00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.640]   is included in SAG's press release today, which, again, is a very important piece of information.
[00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:29.940]   Thank you.
[00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.860]   It can be found on the Investor Relations website.
[00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:37.920]   The non-GAAP information is not a substitute for any performance measure derived in accordance with GAAP,
[00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:42.600]   and the use of such non-GAAP measures has limitations which are detailed in the company's press release.
[00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:45.700]   And now I'd like to turn the call over to Chris Fahar. Chris?
[00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:49.840]   Thanks, Brendan, and thank you to everyone on today's call.
[00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:52.480]   We hope you and your families continue to be safe and healthy.
[00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:56.440]   Firstly, let me start by thanking our entire SAG team across the globe.
[00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:59.780]   I'm extremely proud to see how our teams reacted through the quarter,
[00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.620]   and never lost sight of serving our consumers and partners with quality products that protect and enhance their devices.
[00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:12.560]   Over the course of the third quarter, it was pleasing to see our results improve significantly compared with the second quarter,
[00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.200]   and exceed our expectations.
[00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:21.460]   We are encouraged by our recent performance, given the challenges we continue to face from the ongoing health pandemic and its impact on the economy.
[00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:28.800]   Our work over the past several months, which has included reducing expenses, adapting our operations to the current retail environment,
[00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:29.980]   and aggressively improving our services.
[00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:36.980]   We are also pleased to see that the company managing inventories has put the company in a much stronger financial position and provided the business with good momentum as we head into our busiest selling season.
[00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:43.700]   Looking at our third quarter in more detail, as we discussed on our Q2 call in August,
[00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:53.700]   we saw a significant sequential uptick in sell-through in June for both our protection and power categories as several of our larger customers reopened their doors and resumed more normalised store operations,
[00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:57.080]   with some sell-through weeks even exceeding last year's levels.
[00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:59.960]   This trend continued into July and consistently increased over the last year.
[00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:08.740]   While our online sales growth did temper a bit from levels we experienced early in the pandemic when much of the brick-and-mortar was closed,
[00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:13.840]   it was still up nicely from a year ago, and expanding this channel continues to be a priority for us.
[00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:24.040]   With respect to our overall performance, Q3 revenue came in at $150 million compared to $147 million in the year-ago period, a decrease of 21%.
[00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:29.940]   This represents a nice improvement from the 28% year-over-year decrease in revenue we reported in the second quarter.
[00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:41.940]   Despite the roughly $32 million drop in revenue compared with Q3 of last year, combined with some gross margin headwinds from higher freight expenses, we delivered an adjusted EBITDA of $15 million.
[00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:45.940]   Thanks to the cost-saving measures we enacted early in the pandemic.
[00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:50.940]   Taylor will go through in greater detail on the balance sheet, but I wanted to share a few highlights.
[00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:57.940]   Despite significant market pressure from COVID-19, our accounts receivable DSO has improved compared to last year.
[00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.900]   Inventory declines have also improved.
[00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:02.900]   We have seen a significant decline compared to where we ended Q2.
[00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.900]   We generated positive operating cash flow.
[00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:11.900]   And we continue to reduce our quarter-end net debt balance on a year-over-year and sequential basis.
[00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:18.900]   By taking quick, decisive action back in April, and more recently working closely with our retail partners on their store reopening efforts,
[00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:22.900]   we have been able to successfully navigate through incredibly challenging market conditions,
[00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:29.860]   ensuring the financial viability of the company, and position ourselves to exit this difficult period as a stronger, more nimble organization.
[00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:32.860]   I'll now provide some additional color to our categories.
[00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:34.860]   Starting with protection.
[00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:37.860]   We continue to build on our overall digital wellness strategy.
[00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:40.860]   For a few years now, our hero screen protector has been VisionGuard,
[00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:43.860]   a product that reduces exposure to high-energy visible blue light
